# A record read out of an ordered map, changed, and written back under its
# key, in the shapes the native middle end rewrites and the ones it leaves
# alone: a key read off another record, a block that also reads the map, the
# base or the record read after the write, a renamed base, context or record,
# a record that came from no map, a match with guards, a write inside a
# match's scrutinee, a hash map, and a map held by a name of its own: read out
# by a `let`, by an arm that is no block, read again before the write, under a
# renamed key, or written inside a function made in the arm; a record matched
# out of something else, out of a pair, put back under another key, or written
# with a context made in the arm. Every reader keeps its own view, on both
# backends, and under --coverage, which keeps each context whole.
#
# Schema: the repository-case manifest, cli/tests/harness/case.rs. Textproto,
# but not a Buri file: only repo/ below is a Buri repository.

doc: "a record written back into an ordered map leaves every other holder's view as it was"

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/maps", "--force"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "test.txt"
}

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/maps", "--force", "--coverage"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "covered.txt"
}
